    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example is a gmeow:FlagshipScenario whose gmeow:enforcesFailureClass names logic:Conjecture — a real class that is NOT a logic:LogicConformanceFailure subclass (the failure-range sh:sparql of the slice's thin logic:FlagshipScenarioShape). That constraint fires, so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent (logic:UnwiredFlagshipScenario) — the enforcing failure class is checked by value." .

# =========================================================================== #
# Typed full-FOL IR — procedural constraint projection twins. The positive case
# jointly satisfies all six ontology-authored constraints; each negative fixture
# changes one independent condition and must be rejected by the generated
# sh:SPARQLConstraint surface.
# =========================================================================== #

ex:ecTypedIrConstraintsWellformed a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/typed-ir-constraints-wellformed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The complete implication selects one constructor at every Formula node, carries both ordered operands, and gives each TermCarrier exactly one indexed value kind; its typed literal carries both lexical form and datatype. FormulaConstructorConstraint, both implication guards, TermCarrierValueConstraint, TermCarrierIndexConstraint, and LiteralDatatypeConstraint therefore all remain silent." .

ex:ecTypedIrTwoConstructors a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/typed-ir-two-constructors.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The focus carries both logic:relation and logic:not, so FormulaConstructorConstraint's exactly-one choice is false and its generated SPARQL constraint must reject the ambiguous formula." .

ex:ecTypedIrAntecedentWithoutConsequent a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/typed-ir-antecedent-without-consequent.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The focus selects the implication constructor with logic:antecedent but omits logic:consequent, so ImplicationConsequentConstraint's guarded requirement must reject the incomplete ordered pair." .

ex:ecTypedIrConsequentWithoutAntecedent a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/typed-ir-consequent-without-antecedent.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The focus carries logic:consequent but omits logic:antecedent; its sole counted constructor is logic:relation, isolating the reverse ImplicationAntecedentConstraint guard, which must reject the missing first operand." .

ex:ecTypedIrCarrierTwoValues a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/typed-ir-carrier-two-values.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The indexed TermCarrier simultaneously carries logic:termIri and logic:termVariable, so TermCarrierValueConstraint's exactly-one value-kind choice must reject it." .

ex:ecTypedIrCarrierWithoutIndex a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/typed-ir-carrier-without-index.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The TermCarrier has one unambiguous variable value but no logic:termIndex, so TermCarrierIndexConstraint must reject the positionless RDF argument rather than infer order from serialization." .

ex:ecTypedIrDatatypeWithoutLiteral a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/typed-ir-datatype-without-literal.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The indexed carrier has one IRI value kind plus logic:termLiteralDatatype but no lexical logic:termLiteral, so LiteralDatatypeConstraint must reject the dangling datatype IRI." .

# --- Enactment kernel: the required negatives --------------------------------
#
# One fixture per law, each isolating a single defect. Every kernel constraint
# projects to an sh:SPARQLConstraint, so the code is uniformly
# shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent — which alone cannot prove the SPECIFIC named law
# fired, because EVERY logic:Constraint in the repository shares that component.
# Each cell therefore ALSO pins gmeow:expectedSourceShape: the deterministic
# per-constraint sh:NodeShape the projector mints as
# `{constraint-namespace}{Pascal(local-name)}ProceduralConstraintShape`
# (crates/logic-compile/src/projections/shapes.rs::procedural_shape_iri), which the
# finding carries as its sh:sourceShape. That IRI is unique per law, so the harness
# (crates/slicetest/src/exec.rs, gmeow:expectedSourceShape branch) now rejects a
# fixture that trips a DIFFERENT constraint sharing the generic component code.
#
# SCOPE OF THE PIN — what it does and does not prove. It proves the named law DID
# fire. It does NOT prove nothing else fired: the harness's `violates` branch requires
# only that SOME finding carry the expected code AND originate from the pinned shape;
# it never asserts the finding set is a singleton. The isolation was therefore
# established by MEASUREMENT rather than assumed — each fixture's full finding set was
# enumerated, and ten of the eleven emit exactly one finding, from their own shape.
# The eleventh (ex:ecCompensationAsInverse) emits three, all entailed by its single
# authored defect; its rationale states that outright instead of claiming an isolation
# the data does not have.

ex:ecCheckpointNoFoldedIdentity a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/checkpoint-no-folded-identity.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape logic:CheckpointRestoreIdentityConstraintProceduralConstraintShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A logic:EnactmentCheckpoint with no logic:checkpointDescriptorHash. Restore is identity-gated across seven axes and the fold is what the gate compares first, so an unfolded checkpoint cannot be gated at all. MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent for logic:CheckpointRestoreIdentityConstraint and NO other finding." .

ex:ecContinuationConflated a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/continuation-resume-and-repeat-conflated.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape logic:ContinuationKindDisjointnessConstraintProceduralConstraintShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A continuation record claiming both logic:ContinuationResume and logic:ContinuationRepeat. The two carry different required bindings and different consequences, so a record claiming both has not said which happened. MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent for logic:ContinuationKindDisjointnessConstraint and NO other finding." .

ex:ecPrescriptionNotAddressed a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/prescription-version-not-content-addressed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape logic:PrescriptionVersionImmutabilityConstraintProceduralConstraintShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A logic:PrescriptionVersion with no logic:prescriptionDigest. Immutability is enforced by content addressing rather than a flag, so an unaddressed version makes in-place revision undetectable. MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent for logic:PrescriptionVersionImmutabilityConstraint and NO other finding." .

ex:ecReceiptWithoutAttempt a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/receipt-without-attempt.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape logic:ReceiptRequiresAttemptConstraintProceduralConstraintShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A logic:ExternalEffectReceipt with no logic:receiptOfAttempt, asserting an outcome nobody caused — the shape a fabricated or mis-imported effect record takes. MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent for logic:ReceiptRequiresAttemptConstraint and NO other finding." .

ex:ecUnknownWithoutAttempt a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/unknown-outcome-without-attempt.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape logic:NoBlindRetryConstraintProceduralConstraintShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A logic:ExternalOutcomeUnknown naming no attempt. Retry from an undetermined position is licensed only through the attempt, so this record can never be resolved and can never license the retry it invites. MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent for logic:NoBlindRetryConstraint and NO other finding." .

ex:ecCompensationAsInverse a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/compensation-typed-as-its-forward-receipt.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape logic:CompensationNotInverseConstraintProceduralConstraintShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A logic:CompensationAttempt also typed logic:ExternalEffectReceipt, collapsing the counteraction into the thing counteracted — the guaranteed-inverse reading that makes a failed compensation invisible. MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent from logic:CompensationNotInverseConstraintProceduralConstraintShape, which gmeow:expectedSourceShape pins by IRI. Unlike its ten sibling kernel negatives — each of which was measured to emit EXACTLY ONE finding, its own — this fixture emits THREE, and the rationale says so rather than claiming an isolation the data does not have: the single authored defect (the double typing) CASCADES, because the very act of typing the node logic:ExternalEffectReceipt also puts it in scope of logic:ReceiptRequiresAttemptConstraint (it binds no logic:receiptOfAttempt) while its logic:CompensationAttempt typing puts it in scope of logic:CompensationBindsExactForwardEffectConstraint. The two extra findings are entailed consequences of the ONE defect, not independent breakages, and the source-shape pin is what proves the named law is among those that fired." .

ex:ecCompensationNoReceipt a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/compensation-outcome-without-receipt.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape logic:CompensationSuccessRequiresReceiptConstraintProceduralConstraintShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A logic:CompensationOutcome with no logic:compensationReceipt. Coded separately from the not-an-inverse fixture because the two are independent obligations and a corpus must be able to trip each alone. MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent for logic:CompensationSuccessRequiresReceiptConstraint and NO other finding." .

ex:ecApprovalDetached a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/approval-detached-from-intent.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape logic:ApprovalCommitmentCompletenessConstraintProceduralConstraintShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A logic:ApprovalCommitment binding no logic:approvalIntentDigest. Exact binding is what stops an authorization for one thing licensing another; a commitment with no digest detaches against anything. MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent for logic:ApprovalCommitmentCompletenessConstraint and NO other finding." .

ex:ecAdvisoryAuthorizesPin a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/advisory-authorizes-a-pin.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape logic:AdvisoryNeverAuthorityConstraintProceduralConstraintShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A logic:Advisory occupying the logic:pinAuthority position. Model output is attributed evidence and may never license an action; the separation is structural rather than conventional because a convention is what fails under time pressure. MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent for logic:AdvisoryNeverAuthorityConstraint and NO other finding." .

ex:ecFrontierUnwitnessed a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/frontier-closed-without-saturation-witness.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape logic:FrontierClosureRequiresSaturationConstraintProceduralConstraintShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A logic:ActionableFrontier with no logic:frontierSaturationWitness. An unwitnessed closure claim is exactly how a roster truncated by a budget cut passes for complete, after which the system confidently omits the action it should have taken. MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent for logic:FrontierClosureRequiresSaturationConstraint and NO other finding." .

ex:ecFrontierContentFreeWitness a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/frontier-cites-a-content-free-witness.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape logic:FrontierClosureRequiresSaturationConstraintProceduralConstraintShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A logic:ActionableFrontier citing a logic:SaturationWitness that names no logic:settledPredicate and states no logic:consumedBudget. It passes every law that merely counts the citation, so an operator reads a certified-closed roster backed by evidence that records nothing which could be false. MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent for logic:FrontierClosureRequiresSaturationConstraint and NO other finding." .

ex:ecPinStepsMismatchMethod a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/pin-freezes-steps-its-method-never-yielded.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape logic:PinStepsMatchInstantiatedMethodConstraintProceduralConstraintShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A logic:PinnedExecutableSubgraph whose logic:pinnedStepSequence is not the logic:methodYields sequence of the logic:DecompositionMethod it names. The refinement was validated against one decomposition and the pin dispatches another, so the approval licenses a step nobody reviewed — and every record involved is individually well-formed, which is why only a relational law sees it. MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent for logic:PinStepsMatchInstantiatedMethodConstraint and NO other finding." .

ex:ecCapabilityGapNoStep a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/capability-gap-without-blocked-step.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
